            "value": "Applies when %1$@ games run in %2$@. “Default” leaves %3$@’s own setting as it is."
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "S’applique quand les jeux %1$@ tournent dans %2$@. « Par défaut » laisse le réglage de %3$@ tel quel."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Arcade": {
      "localizations": {
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Arcade"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Arcade DATs": {
      "localizations": {
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "DAT arcade"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Arcade sets are checked against the version of the emulator that runs them: chip by chip, with what a clone takes from its parent and a game from its BIOS set, and each disc image.": {
      "localizations": {
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Les sets arcade sont vérifiés d’après la version de l’émulateur qui les lance : puce par puce, avec ce qu’un clone prend à son parent et un jeu à son set BIOS, et chaque image disque."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Arguments": {
      "localizations": {
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Arguments"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Artwork": {
      "localizations": {
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Illustration"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Assigned Systems": {
      "localizations": {
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Systèmes attribués"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Assign…": {
      "localizations": {
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Attribuer…"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Attic Help": {
      "localizations": {
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Aide d’Attic"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Attic can fetch descriptions, release dates and artwork from ScreenScraper or TheGamesDB. ScreenScraper matches games exactly by file; TheGamesDB searches by title.": {
      "localizations": {
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Attic peut récupérer descriptions, dates de sortie et illustrations depuis ScreenScraper ou TheGamesDB. ScreenScraper identifie les jeux exactement par fichier ; TheGamesDB cherche par titre."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Attic can’t change this emulator’s settings. Set them up in the emulator itself.": {
      "localizations": {
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Attic ne peut pas modifier les réglages de cet émulateur. Configurez-les dans l’émulateur lui-même."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Attic checks your games against No-Intro's lists of known good dumps, the DAT files. Nothing is changed.": {
      "localizations": {
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Attic vérifie vos jeux d’après les listes de bons dumps de No-Intro, les fichiers DAT. Rien n’est modifié."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Attic couldn't write a backup to %@. Check that the folder is there and has room.": {
      "localizations": {
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Attic n’a pas pu écrire de sauvegarde dans %@. Vérifiez que le dossier est là et qu’il reste de la place."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Attic doesn't download DATs itself: No-Intro hands them out through its site only.": {
      "localizations": {
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Attic ne télécharge pas les DAT lui-même : No-Intro ne les distribue que sur son site."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Attic downloads emulators from their official sources only: RetroArch and its cores from libretro's buildbot, standalone emulators from their own release pages. Each system's page lists the recommended emulator first.": {
      "localizations": {
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Attic télécharge les émulateurs uniquement depuis leurs sources officielles : RetroArch et ses cœurs depuis le buildbot de libretro, les émulateurs autonomes depuis leur propre page de versions. La page de chaque système indique d’abord l’émulateur recommandé."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Attic installs blueMSX's machine and database files into the BIOS folder with the core.": {
      "localizations": {
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Attic installe les fichiers de machines et de base de données de blueMSX dans le dossier BIOS avec le cœur."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Attic reads ROMs folders organized the way Batocera, RetroBat and ES-DE do it: one subfolder per system, named after the system (snes, megadrive, neogeo…). Each system's help page lists the folder names it recognizes.": {
      "localizations": {
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Attic lit les dossiers de ROMs organisés comme Batocera, RetroBat et ES-DE : un sous-dossier par système, nommé d’après le système (snes, megadrive, neogeo…). La page d’aide de chaque système indique les noms de dossier reconnus."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "BIOS": {
      "localizations": {
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "BIOS"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "BIOS files": {
      "localizations": {
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Fichiers BIOS"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "BIOS, saves, save states, RetroArch cores and settings, and emulators installed by Attic all live here — back up or move this one folder to take everything with you.": {
      "localizations": {
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Les BIOS, sauvegardes, sauvegardes d’état, cœurs et réglages de RetroArch et les émulateurs installés par Attic sont tous ici — sauvegardez ou déplacez ce seul dossier pour tout emporter."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Back Up Now": {
      "localizations": {
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Sauvegarder maintenant"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Back Up Saves": {
      "localizations": {
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Sauvegarder les parties"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Back up every week": {
      "localizations": {
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Sauvegarder chaque semaine"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Backing up saves…": {
      "localizations": {
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Sauvegarde des parties…"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Backup Failed": {
      "localizations": {
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Échec de la sauvegarde"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Bad dumps": {
      "localizations": {
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Mauvais dumps"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Bottom (A / Cross)": {
      "localizations": {
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Bas (A / Croix)"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Bottom confirms": {
      "localizations": {
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Valider en bas"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Bottom — Xbox, PlayStation": {
      "localizations": {
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "En bas — Xbox, PlayStation"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Brings in the covers, screenshots, videos, manuals and descriptions another front-end has for your games, and the games you don't have if you like.": {
      "localizations": {
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Récupère les jaquettes, captures d’écran, vidéos, manuels et descriptions qu’un autre front-end a pour vos jeux, et si vous le souhaitez les jeux que vous n’avez pas."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Browse": {
      "localizations": {
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Parcourir"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Browse games": {
      "localizations": {
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Parcourir les jeux"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "But not": {
      "localizations": {
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Mais pas"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Button Mapping": {
      "localizations": {
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Attribution des boutons"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Buttons are named like on a Super Nintendo pad, RetroArch's standard. By default games use buttons by position, like the console's own pad: on an Xbox-style pad, a Nintendo game's A is the right button. Applies to every player in RetroArch games, and to DuckStation. Changed buttons are shown in bold.": {
      "localizations": {
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Les boutons sont nommés comme sur une manette Super Nintendo, la référence de RetroArch. Par défaut, les jeux utilisent les boutons selon leur position, comme sur la manette d’origine : sur une manette de type Xbox, le A d’un jeu Nintendo est le bouton de droite. S’applique à tous les joueurs dans les jeux RetroArch, et à DuckStation. Les boutons modifiés sont en gras."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "By default games use buttons by position, like the console's own pad. Button mapping changes which of your controller's buttons does what in RetroArch games, for every player. Select + Start quits a game in RetroArch and DuckStation.": {
      "localizations": {
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Par défaut, les jeux utilisent les boutons selon leur position, comme sur la manette d’origine. L’attribution des boutons change le rôle de chaque bouton de votre manette dans les jeux RetroArch, pour tous les joueurs. Select + Start quitte un jeu dans RetroArch et DuckStation."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "CD": {
      "localizations": {
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "CD"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "CRT TV": {
      "localizations": {
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Téléviseur CRT"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Cabinet Mode": {
      "localizations": {
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Mode Cabinet"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Cabinet Mode (full screen)": {
      "localizations": {
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Mode Cabinet (plein écran)"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Cabinet Mode is a full-screen view made for the TV and a controller. Open it with ⌘⇧B, the Cabinet Mode toolbar button, or Menu / Start on a controller; leave it with the back button.": {
      "localizations": {
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Le mode Cabinet est une vue plein écran pensée pour la télé et une manette. Ouvrez-le avec ⌘⇧B, le bouton Mode Cabinet de la barre d’outils, ou Menu / Start sur une manette ; quittez-le avec le bouton retour."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Cancel": {
      "localizations": {
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Annuler"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Can’t find this shader file.": {
      "localizations": {
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Impossible de trouver ce fichier de shader."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Cartridge games to ZIP": {
      "localizations": {
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Jeux cartouche en ZIP"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Carts are .p8 or .p8.png files, from the PICO-8 website (Splore) or itch.io. Retro8 runs most of them; the official PICO-8 app runs all.": {
      "localizations": {
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Les cartouches sont des fichiers .p8 ou .p8.png, du site de PICO-8 (Splore) ou d’itch.io. Retro8 en fait tourner la plupart ; l’app PICO-8 officielle les fait toutes tourner."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Change any system's choice below.": {
      "localizations": {
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Modifiez le choix de chaque système ci-dessous."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Change…": {
      "localizations": {
